    <briefdescription>
<para>POSIX asynchronous I/O (&lt;<ref refid="aio_8h" kindref="compound">aio.h</ref>&gt;) </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Provides the aiocb control block and the asynchronous I/O functions. Operations are submitted to the OS-managed request pool (CONFIG_SYS_AIO) and performed by a dedicated kernel service queue; completion is observed with <ref refid="group__posix__option__group__asynchronous__io_1ga64d319c5b3bbb17bb6d7abea7bb24a6d" kindref="member">aio_error()</ref>, <ref refid="group__posix__option__group__asynchronous__io_1gaeba1fa0903a60c511db8d887272aedec" kindref="member">aio_suspend()</ref>, and <ref refid="group__posix__option__group__asynchronous__io_1ga407c314becddbc48abff898635458ed8" kindref="member">aio_return()</ref>, or announced by the control block&apos;s sigevent.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ulink url="https://pubs.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/9699919799/basedefs/aio.h.html">POSIX.1-2017 &lt;aio.h&gt;</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
